.nh
.TH "PB-PORT-NAME-UNSET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port-name-unset - Remove a port name


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port name unset <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one port name of the active workspace. Say which one with --machine (a name
of that machine's port), --all-machines or --top-level. The same people who may set a
name may remove it; the port itself and its access do not change.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all-machines\fP[=false]
	name this port on every machine of the workspace

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unset

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	the machine whose port is named

.PP
\fB--top-level\fP[=false]
	make <name>\&.<domain> open the port of --machine


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb port name unset app --machine homelab
  pb port name unset grafana --all-machines
  pb port name unset jellyfin --top-level
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-port-name(1)\fP
